## Location
`rust/lichen-schc/src/codec.rs` lines 95-109 (BitWriter::write) and 127-144 (BitReader::read)

## Issue
Both BitWriter::write() and BitReader::read() iterate one bit at a time through the value. For 128-bit addresses and DODAGIDs, this means 128 loop iterations per field.

## Current code (BitWriter::write)
```rust
for i in (0..nbits).rev() {
    let bit = ((value >> i) & 1) as u8;
    let byte_pos = self.nbits / 8;
    let bit_pos = 7 - (self.nbits % 8);
    // ...
    self.nbits += 1;
}
```

## Suggested fix
When byte-aligned, write/read whole bytes at a time. Only use bit-by-bit for unaligned portions. This reduces O(nbits) to O(nbits/8) for the bulk of the data.

## Impact
For a typical CoAP compress with two 128-bit addresses + ports + CoAP fields, this is ~300+ loop iterations reduced to ~40.
